.env

# Deploy build byproduct (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml)
build/
docker/volumes/postgres_data/**
docker/volumes/php_home/**
# Release signing keys live outside the repo (docs/android_capacitor.md section 6), so this
# matches nothing today. It is here for the day somebody copies one in "just to try it".
*.jks
*.keystore
docker/volumes/node_home/**
# Holds the Android debug keystore, which is a key: kept out of git, but kept across builds
# (docker-compose.yml, service `capacitor`) so the debug APK's signing fingerprint does not
# change. That fingerprint is registered in the Firebase console for native Google sign-in and
# in assetlinks.json for WebAuthn, so a regenerated keystore silently breaks both.
docker/volumes/android_home/**
!docker/volumes/**/.gitkeep
